@startuml
hide circle
hide empty members

class User << (A,#e8f0ff) aggregate root >> {
  id : UUID
  username : Username
  passwordHash : HashedPassword
  enabled : boolean
  createdAt : Instant
  lastLoginAt : Instant
  --
  authenticate(rawPassword) : boolean
  recordSuccessfulLogin()
}

class Username << (V,#fff3d6) value object >> {
  value : String
  --
  {static} of(raw) : Username
}
note right of Username
  Not blank, unique across all
  users. Case-insensitive for
  lookup (stored as entered).
end note

class HashedPassword << (V,#fff3d6) value object >> {
  hash : String
}
note right of HashedPassword
  BCrypt hash only — the raw
  password is never persisted
  or logged. Matches
  PasswordEncoder already used
  by the in-memory user today.
end note

User *-- Username
User *-- HashedPassword

note bottom of User
  This story only needs enough of a User to
  authenticate and to have something to audit
  against later (id, timestamps). Roles /
  permissions are a real requirement mentioned
  for this system, but not one this story
  implements — see "Not in this story" in the
  README. Adding a Role/Permission model later
  should not require reshaping this aggregate,
  just extending it.
end note

@enduml
